led and executed in a sandbox, and you get back what it printed, what it wrote to standard error, how long it took and the exit status. It exists so a product that needs to run code somebody else wrote does not have to build and defend the machine that runs it."},{question:"How is it different from running code on my own servers?",answer:"The hard part of running untrusted code is not running it, it is containing it. Every run needs its own filesystem, its own process limits, no route to your network, and a way to stop a program that never ends. Doing that yourself means maintaining a sandbox and patching it for as long as the feature lives. The API gives you a fresh sandbox per run and someone else keeps it current."},{question:"Which languages does the JDoodle compiler API support?",answer:`JDoodle runs ${qo()}, including every language on the site, so what you can run here you can run from the API. Each one offers several versions, and you choose the version per request rather than being held to whatever is newest.`},{question:"What does the compiler API cost?",answer:"Your plan gives you a number of credits a day, and they reset daily. Running code costs one credit per run, whatever the language. Checking how many credits you have left is free however often you ask. There is a free tier to build against before you commit to anything."},{question:"REST or WebSocket?",answer:"Start with REST. One request, one response with the final output, which is what grading, fixed input and most integrations need. Use the WebSocket when your user has to answer the program while it runs, or when you want output to appear as it is produced rather than at the end. The socket builds on the same request, so moving between them is small."},{question:"Can I let people write code in my own page instead?",answer:"Yes, and if you want the editor as well as the execution, an embed is usually less work than an API. An embedded IDE drops a working editor into your page with no backend of your own. The API is the right choice when you already have an interface and only need the run."}]},integrate:{metaTags:[{name:"description",content:"Put a working code editor in your page, article or course. No backend of your own, no toolchain for the reader, and every language JDoodle runs."},{name:"keywords",content:"Integrate IDE -  LMS integration -  IDE APIs -  IDE Plugins -  compiler -  API -  online programming -  online ide integration"}],title:"Embed an Online IDE in Your Website | JDoodle"},teachassess:{metaTags:[{name:"description",content:"Create an online classroom to manage your students, create courses, exercises, assessments and track their progress. Teach programming online with JDoodle."},{name:"keywords",content:"Education platform -  auto grading -  student assignments -  virtual institute -  programming assessments -  programming courses -  online compiler -  online ide -  LMS integration"}],title:"Virtual Classroom for Teaching & Assessing Code"},educators:{metaTags:[{name:"description",content:"Build your own digital classroom by creating assessments for students and automate grading. Teach coding online with JDoodle's assessment platform."},{name:"keywords",content:"Education platform -  auto grading -  student assignments -  virtual institute -  programming assessments -  programming courses -  online compiler -  online ide -  online programming -  online classroom -  LMS integration"}],title:"Your Virtual Classroom for Online Assessments & Auto-Grading"},edutech:{metaTags:[{name:"description",content:"Easily integrate code execution into your platform with JDoodle's compiler APIs & embeds. Create an intuitive experience for coders."},{name:"keywords",content:"Education technology -  modern learning -  tech solutions -  Integrate compiler IDE -  LMS integration -  compiler IDE APIs -  IDE Plugins -  online compiler -  online IDE"}],title:"Integrate IDE on your platform | JDoodle APIs & Embeds"},libprovider:{metaTags:[{name:"description",co